        "source_sha256": "2b8f6e59e073a3429c00487de27d8da9a8a27ad315c82419591505f9d43d78a8",
        "text": "top of page\nDonate\n###### Invested in Gilroy\n# CHRISTINA\nTOVAR\n###### for\n###### GILROY CITY COUNCIL\n###### DISTRICT 5\n###### Invested in Gilroy\nCHRISTINA TOVAR FOR CITY COUNCIL ★ DISTRICT 5 ★ INVESTED. ENGAGED. COMMITTED. ★\nA campaign rooted here\nREADY TO LEAD\nGilroy is my home. I've raised my four boys here with my loving husband and now I'm watching my grandkids grow up here too. I've invested in Gilroy in a way I'm proud of. I'm a CPA, and I run two small businesses right in the heart of downtown — I bought a building here because I never wanted my headquarters to be anywhere else.\n​\nI've come to learn that success comes down to a few simple things: listen carefully, do what you say you'll do, and work hard for the people counting on you. That's the experience and the work ethic I want to bring to City Hall because I love this city. I'm ready to serve the residents of the community I love.\nMEET CHRISTINA\n## What she's fighting for\n### FISCAL RESPONSIBILITY\nEvery tax dollar should be treated like it came out of your pocket — because it did. As a CPA, I read a budget to find the smartest path to yes, not reasons to say no. That means transparency, discipline, and real results.\n### BACK OUR BUSINESSES\nGilroy's economy grows when the businesses we already have can thrive and downtown gives people reasons to show up. That means cutting red tape, updating outdated zoning to be more community-friendly, and spending locally so our dollars stay here.\n### SUPPORT FIRST RESPONDERS\nThe people who keep us safe deserve our full support — a well-staffed police department, firefighters ready when we call, and real crime prevention. Growing our local revenue lets us fund them the right way, so families feel secure in every neighborhood.\n### TRANSPARENCY\nToo often, residents get \"invited\" to weigh in after the decision's already made and the money's already spent. That's backwards. Real transparency means bringing people in at the start — sharing the plan, asking what we actually want, and treating passionate residents as partners in solving problems, not obstacles to manage. People aren't just frustrated by outcomes. They're frustrated by not being heard.\nGilroy's nonprofits do work that changes lives, and I've been proud to stand alongside them — funding therapy rooms, chairing toy drives, and helping our schools and kids. I know these organizations and the people behind them. As your councilmember, I'll make sure the city treats them as partners, not afterthoughts.\n### COMMUNITY SUPPORT\n## AAUW\n## Rebekah Children's Services\n## Friends of the Gilroy Library\n## Gilroy Police Foundation\n## Mt. Madonna YMCA\nOrganizations I've had the opportunity to support​\n​\n## Gilroy Rodeo\n## GDBA\n## Gilroy Assitance League\n## Gilory Parent Club\n## Gilroy Elk's Lodge\n## Garlic Festival\n## Edward Boss Prado Foundation\n## Gilroy Chamber of Commerce\n## Latino Family Fund\n## Gilroy Sunrise Rotary\n## Gilroy Exchange Club\n## Miller Red Barn\n## Operation Freedom Paws\n## Gilroy Historical Society\n## St. Joseph's\n## One Giving Tree\n## Students of GHS\n## Las Animas Elementary\n## Wounded Warriors\n## Gilroy Foundation\n## She'll fight for us.\n\"I love Gilroy. I've raised my family here, built my businesses here, and supported wherever I could. I want to help Gilroy be the best version of itself.\"\nGET INVOLVED\nbottom of page",
